# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Environment (Supabase credentials — never commit)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# V29: the Vercel CLI's temp env dump lands in the repo root on `vercel env
# pull` and contains a live OIDC token. It was untracked-but-not-ignored, so any
# `git add -A` would have committed a credential.
.vercel-env-tmp.json

# Playwright e2e (V2 ticket 00) — marker storageState (session tokens)
# and test artifacts, never commit
e2e/.auth/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# opencode runtime state (session continuation files — not source)
.omo/

# Visual-check screenshots (regenerate with .scratch/v4/shot.mjs)
.scratch/**/*.png

# Verification artifacts that can carry a live session token — never commit
.scratch/**/marker-state.json

# Jev QA lane (scripts/qa-jev.sh) — the pinned jev-ultrafast clone, its uv venv,
# the clean Chrome profile, and the NInfer key (.qa/ninfer.env) are all local and
# must never ship. The reproducible model.py fix lives in scripts/qa-jev.patch
# (tracked) and is re-applied over the pinned commit each bootstrap.
.qa/

# Throwaway commit-message files written by the agent loop
.scratch/**/*.txt

# Throwaway probe/scratch scripts and generated review pages. These are the
# V18 lesson: the clean-range check (.scratch/check-push-range.sh) FAILED on
# them, because a probe script written to answer one question during a slice is
# not source and must never ride a push. The durable scripts that ARE source
# live in scripts/ and are tracked deliberately.
.scratch/**/*.cjs
.scratch/**/*.mjs
.scratch/**/*.html

# `.agents/` is local-only agent workspace, named in `.scratch/check-push-range.sh`
# as a forbidden pushed path (docs/agents/auto-push.md rule 2) — so it needs the
# same ignore rule the check already assumes. It was missing, which is how
# `product-marketing.md` got as far as a commit on 2026-09-23: the check caught
# it, but only after `git add`. Ignoring it makes the commit impossible instead.
.agents/

# Vitest's own cache directory. Never source, never committed.
.vitest/

# The Chrome profile / uv cache the sandbox forces into the workspace (the
# home-directory equivalents are read-only under workspace-write).
.scratch/**/chrome-profile/
.scratch/**/chrome-config/
.scratch/**/chrome-cache/
.scratch/**/uv-cache/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# V7 design exploration — local-only mockups used to pick the palette and the
# mark. Scratch, not product.
#
# V22 slice 3: the two HTML mockups USED to live under public/, where Vite
# copied them into dist/ and they would have shipped in any deploy made by
# uploading that directory. They now live in .scratch/design-mockups/, which the
# `.scratch/**/*.html` rule below already covers, so their explicit public/ paths
# are gone from this file — a stale ignore entry for a path that no longer exists
# reads as a live safeguard and is worse than no entry at all.
logo-mockup.png

# NOTE: scripts/crop-*-harness.html are deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. They are
# dev-only HTML (Vite serves them in dev; they are not build inputs, so they never
# ship) and they are the reproducible evidence for the crop step's central claim —
# that the frame the dialog shows is the frame the encoder keeps. Ignoring them
# would leave that claim unverifiable by anyone else.

# machine-local provider config (local API key + Tailscale URL — never commit)
opencode.json
.vercel

# Supabase CLI local state (machine-specific: linked project ref, cached CLI
# version). Never version-control -- see V16 t07 item 3 review.
supabase/.temp/

# A literal `~/` directory: the result of a shell that failed to expand a tilde
# (e.g. `--user-data-dir=~/.hermes/...` inside a quoted string). On 2026-09-21
# one existed here holding a 6.7MB copy of the headless Chrome profile, and it
# pulled browser binaries into every lint scan. Never a source file.
~/

.scratch/**/ocr-*.json

# Factory runtime exhaust — reservations and the two logs. Not record: WORK STATE
# (factory/work/) and DECISIONS (the batch ledger) are the record, and both are
# tracked. See docs/agents/factory.md.
factory/state/
factory/logs/
